    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** edits one picture from a written instruction with LongCat-Image-Edit-Turbo (6B, Apache-2.0, 8 steps). The picture keeps its shape. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Your picture**: the picture to edit. It is set to `example.png` (ships with ComfyUI) so the first Run works.\n   - **Edit instruction**: say what to change and what to keep. Text that must appear goes in \"quotes\".\n   - **Megapixels** (1): size of the result. The picture is resized to this many pixels, shape kept, sides rounded to 16 (1776x1184 in gives 1248x832). Small pictures are enlarged.\n   - **Steps** (8): what the authors made the Turbo model for.\n   - **Seed**: fixed at 25112026. Type a new number for another take; Run with nothing changed does nothing.\n2. **Models**: the three loaders must show the files from the Downloads note.\n3. **Picture + instruction**: nothing to change.\n4. **Sampling**: CFG 1, euler / simple. Nothing to change; the Turbo model has no negative prompt.\n5. **Save**: press **Run**. The result is saved to `output/LongCat/`.\n\n**What to expect:** a 1248x832 result in 27 to 28 s on the test card (8 steps); the default `example.png` gives 1024x1024 in 28 s.\nParts the instruction does not name can still change: writing a word on a blurred hedge also redrew the hedge.\n\n**Tested on:** RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, 64 GB RAM, ComfyUI 0.45.3. Not verified on a 12 GB card.\n"
   ]
  },
